{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Refactor SuperAdminDashboard",
  "description": "Split SuperAdminDashboard into smaller components",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "userTriggered"
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "Refactor the SuperAdminDashboard.tsx file at procurement-fe/src/components/superadmin/SuperAdminDashboard.tsx into smaller, more maintainable components.\n\nThe file is currently 786+ lines and does too much. Break it into:\n\n1. A main dashboard component that orchestrates everything\n2. Separate components for:\n   - Statistics cards display\n   - Admin management table (with create/edit/delete)\n   - Users table\n   - Vendors table\n   - Tenders table\n   - Modal forms (create admin, edit admin role, delete confirmation)\n\nFollow this structure:\n- procurement-fe/src/components/superadmin/\n  - SuperAdminDashboard.tsx (main component)\n  - AdminManagement.tsx (admin CRUD table + create/edit modals)\n  - StatCards.tsx (statistics cards)\n  - UsersTable.tsx (user listing)\n  - VendorsTable.tsx (vendor listing)\n  - TendersTable.tsx (tender listing)\n  - modals/\n    - CreateAdminModal.tsx\n    - EditAdminRoleModal.tsx\n    - DeleteAdminModal.tsx\n\nEach component should have its own props, state, and logic. Extract reusable patterns. Use TypeScript interfaces for all props.\n\nReturn a summary of what was created."
  }
}